  "notes": "Historical-year build for the 2023-2024 catalog, mirroring SRA-2026.json's already-verified Intelligence Analysis and Modeling Option plan. Verified by fetching this year's real archived bulletin page (raw HTML, not WebFetch's summarizer) at the source URL above and cross-checking its printed 'Program Requirements' course list and 'Suggested Academic Plan' semester table against SRA-2026.json's own plan -- the Intelligence Analysis and Modeling Option's required-course list, credit values, and 8-semester structure are functionally identical to 2026's for this catalog year (same Prescribed/Additional Courses in the Common Requirements section: IST 110/210/432/495, SRA 111/211/231, STAT 200, ENGL 202C/202D, PSYCH 100/SOC 5, ECON 102/104/AGBM 101, MATH 22/26/40/41/110/140, PLSC 1/14/GEOG 128, SRA 365/STAT 460, IST 140/CMPSC 101/121; same Option course list: IST 452, SRA 268, SRA 311W, SRA 421, SRA 433, SRA 440W, SRA 468, plus 15 credits of Supporting Courses at least 3 of which are 400-level). Differences found were cosmetic bulletin-boilerplate only (entrance-to-major minimum GPA text, General Education Foundations/Knowledge-Domains wording, course-title-only changes like SOC 5's retitling, administrative-enrollment-control dates) and do not change this plan's schedulable course list or credits, so this file otherwise mirrors SRA-2026.json's own fixes verbatim: the real STAT 200 'Placement into MATH 21 or higher' prereq (confirmed unchanged for this year via the archived STAT course-description page) still needs the MATH 3 -> MATH 4 -> MATH 21 chain waived per planner_engine.expand_math_placement(), so MATH 21 alone is kept as a scheduled item and MATH 3/MATH 4 are correctly omitted (same staleness fix already applied to 2026); SRA 433's real 'SRA 211 and SRA 221 and SRA 231 and SRA 311' prereq (confirmed unchanged via the archived SRA course-description page) still needs SRA 311 as a second option alongside SRA 311W; and the 4 Supporting Course slots keep the same ist.psu.edu support-of-option match list and the 6 GEN ED / 2 US-or-IL slot domain wiring, since nothing found in this year's bulletin suggests either changed. REAL DIFFERENCE FOUND (course renumbering): same as 2022 -- 'CYBER 221' did not exist yet this year (confirmed absent from the archived 2023-24 CYBER course-description page; the bulletin's own Common Requirements list shows 'SRA 221' alone). Semester 3's item nonetheless keeps the CYBER 221/SRA 221 pair, for the identical reason documented in SRA-2022.json's notes: the engine's catalog is scraped from the CURRENT live bulletin only, which has fully renumbered this course to CYBER 221 (SRA 221 no longer exists there), and SRA 433/SRA 440W's real prereq_groups require CYBER 221 literally -- confirmed by running build_full_plan with SRA 221 modeled alone, which produced real 'Could not schedule: SRA 433, SRA 440W' warnings. Pair kept, labeled 'CYBER 221 (or legacy SRA 221)', matching CMPSC's legacy-code convention.",
